    "body": "DUNCAN_NIGHT_REPORT_R01\nCYCLE_ID = DNR01-20260902-011\nMODE = LEARNING_RUNTIME_REGRESSION_REPAIR_CYCLE\nSOURCE_WINDOW = 2026-09-02 / repeated live decision-regression diagnosis\nMAIN_HEAD_OBSERVED = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1\nPRIME_CORE_CHANGED = NO\nPRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO\nDAY_EVENTS_REVIEWED = issue #206 Night School/Fortress contract and prior terminal evidence; issue #251 current single-product routing; current zb-archive-v1 head 2524116f621650936fec289434d932e20adff707; current DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT latest_cycle_id DNR01-20260831-010; PR #209 merged Fortress R01 scope; current main AGENTS/Constitution fresh-read\nANIME_TOPICS_STUDIED = operational animation-production decision discipline only; no new aesthetic threshold promoted\nOPEN_SOURCE_CODE_INSPECTED = current main scripts/duncan_night_archive.py and PR #209 scope. The implementation validates/archives DUNCAN_NIGHT_REPORT_R01 and rebuilds hq/archive-v1/derived/duncan-night-v1/DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT.json, but current evidence does not show a mandatory live-session consumer that reads that derived context before tool/action selection.\nEXERCISES = classify the OWNER bounded goal `simple Duncan animation -> 3-4 key drawings/poses -> inbetweens for smoothness` without inventing a new shot, dashboard, source/Krita gate, or unrelated image-generation task; separately classify the OWNER diagnosis request `learning/intelligence appears not to work` as a runtime-learning repair task rather than production-image generation.\nVERIFICATION = fresh archive read proves DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT exists and is rebuildable but latest_cycle_id is DNR01-20260831-010; fresh automation inventory shows no active task titled Duncan Anime Night School; current live failure history demonstrates stored context/corrections did not prevent repeated process substitution and tool-before-task classification errors.\nFAILURES = repeated stale-route resurrection; over-formalizing a bounded animation goal; invoking image generation when the OWNER was asking for workflow/repair rather than a requested image artifact; treating persistence/rebuildability PASS as if it proved live cognitive consumption.\nROOT_CAUSES = learning persistence and learning consumption were conflated. The archive path is write/derive/verify capable, but the mandatory ZORR bootstrap did not require fresh-reading DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT before action selection. Same-session OWNER corrections also lacked an explicit immediate-application gate. The historical Night School scheduler is not currently present in the active automation inventory, so context freshness stopped at 2026-08-31.\nREGRESSION_RESULTS = current repair route stopped image/tool execution, fresh-read exact durable learning evidence first, isolated the persistence-vs-consumption boundary, and created a RED test requiring a runtime consumption hook. This is repair evidence only, not a PROVEN skill.\nTRANSFER_TEST = changed/unseen current request `learning intelligence` was routed to diagnosis and minimal runtime wiring rather than to image generation, shot selection, canon search, or a new architecture. One transfer is insufficient for PROVEN.\nSKILL_DELTA =\n- owner_intent_execution_discipline: UNTESTED -> FAILED\nSELF_MODEL_DELTA =\n- LEARNING_CONSUMPTION_RULE = Durable learning is useless at decision time unless the current session explicitly consumes the relevant derived context before selecting a tool/action; persistence PASS must never be promoted to runtime-intelligence PASS.\n- TOOL_CLASSIFICATION_RULE = Classify the OWNER-requested result before invoking a tool; do not invoke image generation for workflow, diagnosis, planning, or repair requests.\n- SIMPLE_GOAL_RULE = Do not expand a bounded OWNER production goal into unnecessary global phases, dashboards, source/runtime proofs, or process ceremonies.\n- IMMEDIATE_CORRECTION_RULE = Apply an explicit OWNER correction on the next case in the same session; Night School consolidates reusable learning later and is not a reason to delay the correction.\nOWNER_TASTE_MODEL_DELTA =\n- RESULT_OVER_PROCESS = CONFIRMED_SUPPORTING_SIGNAL only: repeated explicit OWNER corrections plus existing Constitution product-first law require direct bounded progress and reject process/dashboard/tool ceremony that substitutes for the requested result; not an OWNER lock and not permission to skip necessary quality work.\nCYCLE_RESULT = LEARNING_RUNTIME_REGRESSION / REPAIR_CANDIDATE\nPASS_SCOPE = NONE. This report records a real failure and repair hypothesis. It does not claim runtime-learning PASS, model-weight training, production PASS, canon mutation, or autonomous consciousness.",
